"""A capability/responsibility and governed-preposition detector.

The largest negative signals are 'capable of' and 'responsible for'. Smaller
signals mark familiar adjective/verb complements such as 'associated with'.
Rounded strengths also cover the cue words themselves, a few translations,
and broad pronoun/participle environments, plus fixed Arabic-preposition
offsets. Object-complement phrases can
intervene between a governor and its preposition. Other lexical variation
is ignored.
