"""Respond most strongly to indented code, especially `if`, loops and `try`.

The three calibrations are ordinary spaced text, a bare token, and an
indented statement. The last token's whitespace, its width, and a token's
own leading tab adjust this response. Common programming constructions
get separate estimates. State is just the previous token and document label,
reset at document boundaries. Weak miscellaneous lexical responses are omitted.
No parsing, model computation or lookahead is used.
