  anything, still, even, ...): mildly negative (-0.04).
- English "other"-type words (other, another, some, most, until, though) and "while":
  mildly positive (+0.05 and +0.08).
- Every other token: 0.

It does not model the many small idiosyncratic token effects, so it explains only about
1 to 2 percent of the variance. A full token table would explain much more (the top 1000
tokens' mean activations alone explain about 17 percent in-sample), but it has no concept
behind it.
"""

READS = ()

TEACHING = {"学生", "教师", "教学", "师生", "合作", "激发", "课堂", "引导", "调动"}
TOOL_MARKUP = {"<tool_call>"}
THINK_TAGS = {"<think>", "</think>"}
QUANTIFIERS_NEG = {
    " any", " no", " every", " either", " neither", " nor", " nothing", " anything",
    " everything", " everyone", " anyone", " anywhere", " nobody", " anybody", " still", " even",
}
QUANTIFIERS_POS = {" other", " another", " others", " some", " most", " until", " though"}


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    token = prefix.token_strings[prefix.position]
    if token in TEACHING:
        value = -0.23
    elif token in THINK_TAGS:
        value = -0.2
    elif token in TOOL_MARKUP:
